[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3708391136","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114602#issuecomment-3708391136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114602","id":3708391136,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dCY7g","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-04T20:14:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-04T20:14:36Z","body":"Transparent objects don't get rendered to the normal-roughness buffer since they are rendered after everything else. \n\nThis is a limitation of transparent objects that should be noted here in the docs https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.html","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3708391136/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3708520399","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114602#issuecomment-3708520399","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114602","id":3708520399,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dC4fP","user":{"login":"tripodsan","id":917628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNzYyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/917628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan","html_url":"https://github.com/tripodsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-04T23:20:11Z","updated_at":"2026-01-04T23:28:45Z","body":"> Transparent objects don't get rendered to the normal-roughness buffer since they are rendered after everything else.\n\nthanks @clayjohn. I'm creating a post processing compositor that needs the depth and normal buffer; with the transparent objects, the normal buffer is not there and I don't know how to \"mask out\" the parts I don't need.\n\nI thought I can do a trick with the stencil buffer, but I think this is not available in shader materials yet.\n\nbtw: I also tried to write to `DEPTH` in the fragment shader of the transparent object together with `depth_prepass_alpha`, in the hope that it would then \"ignore\" the depth information of the transparent parts; but this doesn't update the depth buffer.\n\nalso, I just saw that this is a duplicate of [93217](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/93217)\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3708520399/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709829633","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114602#issuecomment-3709829633","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114602","id":3709829633,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dH4IB","user":{"login":"tripodsan","id":917628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNzYyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/917628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan","html_url":"https://github.com/tripodsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tripodsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T10:24:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T10:42:44Z","body":"additional information: \n\nwith `depth_prepass_alpha`, the documentation says:\n> Depth Pre-Pass: This renders the object's fully opaque pixels via the opaque pipeline first, then renders the rest with alpha blending.\n\nthis works (unless the albedo color has an alpha < 1.0). but texture with semi transparent pixels work:\n\n<img height=\"600\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52769d2e-df78-4422-8050-f78afb932cd2\" />\n\nalso, the outline postprocessing works, but what I want to achieve is to ignore the outline on the transparent cutouts:\n\n<img height=\"600\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/78a38cf4-2cc5-40e5-9da9-29bd12047886\" />\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709829633/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]